---
import CodeBlock from '../../../components/CodeBlock.astro'
import DocsLayout from '../../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro'
import { streamExample } from '../../../lib/api-reference.js'
import { sitePath } from '../../../lib/paths.js'
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Live streaming"
  description="Publish native CEF video and page audio to RTMP or RTMPS."
  section="streaming"
>
  <h1>Native live streaming</h1>
  <h2 id="publish-a-page">Publish a page</h2>
  <CodeBlock code={streamExample} />
  <h2 id="stream-options">Stream options</h2>
  <p>
    Set an RTMP/RTMPS URL, output size, output FPS 1–120, boolean audio, bitrate, adaptive bitrate
    and reconnect policy. Source switching requires matching dimensions and pixel format; capture
    rates may differ.
  </p>
  <h2 id="page-audio">Page audio</h2>
  <p>
    Audio comes from CEF callbacks as 48 kHz stereo PCM. It is disabled by default. Timestamped
    buffering aligns it with the video timeline; missing audio contributes silence.
  </p>
  <h2 id="adaptive-bitrate">Adaptive bitrate</h2>
  <p>
    The persistent publisher supports bitrate changes and monitors congestion. Health reports expose
    capture/output lag and progress age.
  </p>
  <h2 id="reconnect-and-stop">Reconnect and stop</h2>
  <p>
    The publisher supervises reconnects. The application owns its source and observes both source
    and publisher failure. A failed source holds its last frame until replacement or stop.
  </p>
  <h2 id="live-effects">Live effects</h2>
  <p>
    Browser-rendered highlights and captions reach captured frames. Offline zoom and the renderer's
    narration mix do not transform a concurrent broadcast.
  </p>
  <h2 id="verify-locally">Verify locally</h2>
  <CodeBlock label="Terminal" code={'pnpm test:native:cadence\npnpm test:native:stream'} />
  <p>
    The stream verifier needs the built native browser and checks decoded received media, source
    replacement and receiver reconnection. Streaming throughput at 120 FPS remains unverified;
    measured recording throughput is on the <a href={sitePath('/docs/performance')}
      >performance page</a
    >.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
